<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lithuanian Riflemen's Union</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1919">1919</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lithuanian Riflemen's Union is a paramilitary volunteer organisation founded in 1919 by Vladas Putvinskis to support the army during the wars of independence. Between the wars it grew into a mass organisation and took part in the seizure of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/klaipeda">Klaipėda</a> in 1923; it was banned in 1940 under Soviet occupation, and many members joined the anti-Soviet resistance. Re-established in 1989, it now forms part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>'s national defence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lithuanian-riflemens-union.jpg" alt="Lithuanian Riflemen's Union" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lithuanian Riflemen's Union · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Insignia_of_%C5%A0auli%C5%B3_s%C4%85junga.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Lithuanian army was founded on 23 November 1918, largely from volunteers, and the <b>Riflemen’s Union</b>, a paramilitary volunteer force, followed in 1919.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-lithuania">Republic of Lithuania · Military</a></li></ul></section>
